# Generalized changes decision log

When you ship a change that is a **key architectural decision** for this portfolio—not every tweak, and not personal taste—append a step to:

[`src/data/content.ts`](src/data/content.ts) → `generalizedChangesMarkdown` (card **Generalized changes** under How this site works).

Do this in the **same change set** as the code when practical.

## When to log

Log if the decision is primarily one or more of:

| Category | Include |
| --- | --- |
| **Structural** | Layout shells, modal scroll model, portals vs in-flow, shared chrome/layout contracts |
| **Device** | Mobile/desktop/fullscreen/orientation behavior, viewport workarounds that become policy |
| **Performance** | Scroll/compositor strategy, prewarm, resize policy, caching/asset strategy that others must follow |
| **Feature** | Gating, unlock/capability rules, dual-mode product behavior, cross-cutting feature contracts |

Skip (do **not** log) personal or content-only preference, for example:

- “This photo makes me look weird” / “I have a better picture”
- Pure copy tone without a behavior or architecture change
- One-off visual preference that does not establish a reusable rule

Not every commit or iteration needs an entry. Prefer logging when a future agent/human should **match or avoid** the pattern.

## Step shape (required)

Newest steps go **at the top** of the `# Decision log` section (below the intro / criteria).

```markdown
## YYYY-MM-DD — <short decision title>

### Category
Structural | Device | Performance | Feature (one or more)

### Decision
What we chose, changed, or queued. Name surfaces/files in backticks when helpful.

### Reason
Why—in engineering/product terms (constraints, consistency, platform limits). No personal aesthetics-as-rationale.
```

- **Decision** = the rule or behavior (or “queued” / “documented only”).
- **Reason** = non-personal justification.
- Do **not** invent fake shipped work—if research-only, say so under **Decision**.

## Relationship to other logs

- **ADA example awareness** (`adaPerfectionMarkdown`) — ADA Guy / accessibility refinements only; keep using that for ADA steps.
- **Generalized changes** — cross-cutting architecture going forward; this log **started after** most of the original build.
- Hero-unit narrative articles can stay educational; durable *policy* decisions that apply beyond one article should also appear here when they meet the criteria.

## Complements

- After site-affecting edits, follow `verify-build-before-resting` (build + static preview).
- `modal-chrome-padding.mdc` / `video-modal-layout.mdc` — still apply until an explicit generalized-changes entry supersedes them.
`)